{"trans": "We advocate for fair competition and oppose deceit and trickery, promoting a diverse and thriving online community. We also promote unity and cooperation, rejecting behavior that harms others for personal gain, and work towards a mutually beneficial and win-win environment on the internet."}
{"trans": "In summary, perhaps more foreign companies believe that listing in the United States is not worth the effort and therefore choose to withdraw as the best option. However, this by no means means that they are ready to give up on the U.S. market."}
{"trans": "He believes that in such a highly volatile market environment, it is extremely difficult for gold to remain unscathed, and any talk of breaking through the $1,000 mark is probably just another pipe dream."}
{"trans": "The police officer explained that the behavior of these students was an act of bravery and righteousness. They stepped forward at a critical moment when the elderly person was in danger of drowning, which is truly commendable. It is understood that the elderly person suffered from a mild mental illness, but after the hospital’s full efforts in rescue, their condition has stabilized and they are now out of danger."}
{"trans": "Of course, the methods mentioned above are just a few of the limited and effective approaches that can be used during revision. The way in which the revision sprint is organized should be diverse and varied, and choices should also be made in consideration of the individual characteristics of each candidate. I wish all candidates the best of success in their endeavors!"}
{"trans": "It has turned into another long river in this very life and era—the very place where Zhaojun dismounted from her horse. The stones upon which she rode still seem to be “talking”; the grass is as green as it was back then, and the flowers carry the fragrance of the past. A herd of cattle and sheep, no longer recognizing the present, bow their heads in humility and caution. In the meticulous passage of time, people drink water and remember its source. Sitting amidst the fragrance of wine, one contemplates the autumn waters of South Lake, the night sky smokeless…"}
{"trans": "This belief is not about seeking to be filled with food all day long, nor about seeking a long life of a hundred years. One cannot live twice; therefore, how can one make the most of the meaning and value of life before death? Even if one is shattered into pieces, one should leave a resounding echo like a piece of jade hitting the ground, producing a metallic sound, and burst forth with the light of life in this world."}
{"trans": "While the others were able to remain calm, holding their guns and observing the enemy surroundings, Li Wenbin was in a complete mess. He dived into the bushes, with his bottom sticking out high, and covered his head with both hands, looking extremely embarrassed. His companions couldn’t help but cover their mouths and laugh at him, causing his reputation to plummet instantly."}
{"trans": "“How do you plan to be a king?” the animals asked, half-believing. “First of all, I will mediate disputes impartially, fairly, and justly. Secondly, I will manage state affairs diligently and without complaint. Thirdly, in the face of a powerful enemy, I will lead from the front and charge into battle. That is my speech on how I will govern.”"}
{"trans": "He is worldly-wise, having experienced the vicissitudes of life for a long time, and is able to turn in the direction like a compass needle. His “north star” (the guiding principle in his life) is unpredictable and not fixed. Thanks also to his charming and flattering words, he remains so insidious that he has never suffered any misfortune. Moreover, he is a eloquent speaker who talks non-stop (unless he hasn’t been paid enough)."}
{"trans": "The first time I followed my colleague to the stock exchange, it was fate that bound me to a lifelong connection with stocks. Over seventeen years, through the ups and downs of spring, summer, autumn, and winter, I have experienced all the joys and sorrows of the stock market. After many trials and tribulations, I have become a veteran in this field, with all those memories still vivid in my mind. One thing is certain: the sea of suffering is endless, but looking back is the way to the shore."}
{"trans": "The remnants of the defeated army fled for a long time before finally stopping. Looking up to the sky, he sighed, “I raised an army at the age of twenty-five; I was invincible in battle and unstoppable in my conquests. Now, in my twilight years, I have suffered such a crushing defeat… It’s truly killing me!” The good news of the victory in the Ningyuan defense battle reached the imperial court, and everyone there was overjoyed. They raised their cups to celebrate."}
{"trans": "In the early days of their marriage, a steady stream of relatives and friends came to offer their blessings. Since the layout of the living room should not be too unconventional, comfort and warmth should be the main priorities. It is important to make the space comfortable for the newlyweds themselves as well as to create a welcoming atmosphere for their guests. Soft, fabric sofas and cushions are essential elements in such a setting."}
{"trans": "I said, “Let’s not overgeneralize; let’s just talk about the specific issue at hand.” My son replied, “For many years, I’ve watched your attitude with a sense of detachment, and I think you’ve made the computer too sacred—a thing that can’t be touched or moved in any way. The biggest obstacle for mothers when it comes to learning is treating the computer like a deity.”"}
{"trans": "Always living in fear, worried about saying the wrong thing, doing the wrong thing, or offending someone. Throughout his life, Zhu Bajie (the seventh of the Eight Immortals) was plagued by sorrow, as many unfortunate events kept coming to mind, inevitably leading to feelings of grief. Zhu Bajie, being highly suspicious, always believed that others were plotting against him, and had to be cautious with every word and action he uttered. As a result, he was restless and frequently suffered from insomnia."}
{"trans": "In that previous, despicable corner, there was also a pitiful guillotine—sneaking around, nervous and embarrassed, as if always in fear of being caught doing something wrong. After each “act,” it would quickly make its escape. How could one not feel relieved by all of this?"}
{"trans": "At this moment, the true charm of fighting lies in the anticipation of battle before the duel, the tense atmosphere before the fight itself, the verbal battles during attempts to mediate, the lively gatherings after the fight, the deep friendship when they meet again, and the side-by-side combat during subsequent encounters. As this cycle repeats, the ranks of pacifists grow stronger and stronger."}
{"trans": "The baron’s utterly shameless insults are simply unbearable; just wait, you contemptible madman. For the sake of honor, I will take it upon myself to avenge this. Only he can bear the responsibility for such blatant insults from everyone around him; I would not tolerate it even if it meant losing my life."}
{"trans": "It doesn’t seem like there will be any arguments or a storm; the situation is now calm and peaceful. Yet, once again, my mother asks an inappropriate question: “Do you want to see what I looked like at your age?” Her daughter’s response is also strange and inappropriate: “Later, dear mom, we can look at it later.”"}
{"trans": "In terms of dealing with people and society, I am still in the beginner stage, but when it comes to knowledge, I am quite confident. No matter how eloquent the department head may be, they might not be more cunning or peculiar than the professors during a master’s thesis defense. If you ask a woodcutter how to eat Western food, they might be at a loss; but if you ask them how to chop wood, that’s surely something they can do effortlessly, right?!"}
{"trans": "“You will soon reap the consequences of your laziness and idleness,” the plow ox said. Then it lowered its head back under the yoke and continued to pull the cart loaded with fertilizer. You should live a life of integrity and always be mindful not to be lazy or idle. If you still don’t find this shameful, then you will surely suffer the consequences of your own actions."}
{"trans": "Draw it, and draw it so vividly and realistically that it seems to come to life. His art has time and again deceived people’s eyes, making them mistake it for a real object at first glance, without realizing that it’s just a painting. For hundreds of years, the art of painting had been considered lowbrow and unsuitable for high society; it was only in his hands that it was revived and brought to new prominence."}
{"trans": "Throughout history, emperors have often been deified, regarded as sacred and inviolable, mysterious and unfathomable, and thus worshipped as if they were gods, which is why they were called “Heavenly Sons.” In reality, emperors were also human beings, with both good and bad qualities. Among them were wise rulers who brought peace and stability to their nations, as well as incompetent and foolish rulers."}
{"trans": "There was a time when he would “walk out the door, laughing heartily at the sky” and chant, “How could we be mere commoners?” The deceit and treachery in the officialdom, the pretense of virtue in the secular world, and the heartless reality chilled his passionate spirit. How could the golden guise of a “imperial court literati” conceal your unrestrained and free-spirited nature? Eventually, after experiencing setbacks and pain in his career, you found peace of mind."}
{"trans": "“A suspicious vagrant has been harassing our territory for some time; he stirs up trouble and sows discord. You are ordered to capture this troublemaker by tomorrow and execute him.” “We will certainly do as you command, sir.” With that, the police officers left. The villain was one-eyed and did not notice the winks and gestures they exchanged while responding to his orders."}
{"trans": "Americans have never deified their national leaders, nor have they ever been willing to follow their commands blindly. However, Obama succumbed to the expectations of his supporters. He also believed that he was the long-awaited savior. The silence of the people was a blow to him. Yet, the feeling of achieving success overnight was so intoxicating that it almost made him lose his sense of reality."}
{"trans": "The ordinary, always smiling Taurus man, with his down-to-earth personality, cannot tolerate the betrayal of those who are two-faced. Don’t try to fathom his true feelings; the steady and reliable Taurus is content with grazing and eating grass. He smiles at you just the way Jesus looks upon his sheep. If you don’t want to turn the camera towards a Spanish bullfighting arena, where blood flows like rivers and carnage is all around, then by all means, don’t make him jealous."}
{"trans": "Without using some little tricks and cunning strategies, Gemini would never find any joy in life. Although they usually seem carefree, once the situation becomes complex, they can strike unexpectedly, leaving everyone battered and wounded while they reap the benefits. But once they successfully capture everyone’s attention, they simply walk away with grace, playing a game of leading you on before pulling back."}
{"trans": "In essence, since Germany is part of the eurozone and thus tied to the euro, the idea that Germany could remain unscathed is simply wishful thinking. The eurozone was created with the grand vision of shared prosperity; now, the Greek debt crisis has triggered a broader European debt crisis, and it’s only natural that everyone suffers together. When one part of the community is in trouble, it affects everyone else. Moreover, the situation around Germany is extremely volatile, with some areas on the brink of becoming wastelands."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, directly investing in commodities might be the most straightforward and effective way to protect against inflation. However, when it comes to commodity investing, the first things that come to mind are often some alarming stories: people who lost all their savings by speculating in commodity futures, and airlines that suffered huge losses from hedging their crude oil positions. These examples make commodity investing seem incredibly risky and daunting to the average person."}
{"trans": "The vast sky endures the fury of lightning and thunder, allowing for calm winds and sunny days; the expansive sea endures the wildness of waves, resulting in gentle ripples; the silent forest endures the cruelty of the survival of the fittest, creating a symphony of birdsong and the fragrance of flowers. It is precisely because the sky, the sea, and the forest know how to tolerate, to yield at the right time, and to humble themselves in acceptance that they possess such beauty and uniqueness. When one humbles themselves, the world seems to grow wider."}
{"trans": "Looking at the rapid changes in the college entrance examination over the past few years, what we need to do is to firmly grasp the new trends and developments in the examination questions. By planning in advance and moving from a state of confusion to a clear understanding of the situation, we can be equipped with the knowledge and skills to face the challenges with ease. With the guidance of experienced teachers, even the simplest tasks can yield remarkable results. A journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step; a nine-story tower is built from a pile of earth. Let us help you take the first step towards success in your college entrance examination preparation!"}
{"trans": "Learning to appreciate yourself is like possessing the golden key to happiness. Appreciating yourself does not mean being self-admiring in a narcissistic way, nor does it mean being arrogant or indulgent in oneself. It certainly does not mean becoming complacent and stopping progressing. Give yourself some confidence, some joy, and a smile. Why worry about not finding happiness in life? Often, you should treat yourself to a celebration and learn to find moments of pleasure."}
{"trans": "Perhaps it’s gradually becoming clear to everyone that the internet and traditional industries are not mortal enemies in a clash of titans, but rather a perfect match, a “pair of outstanding partners.” The retail industry is increasingly showing signs of channel integration, with more and more cross-penetration and combination between online and offline activities. Currently, Taobao has opened physical stores, and traditional companies are also entering the internet arena in large numbers—ranging from Gome, Suning Appliance to Walmart, and Carrefour supermarkets, among others."}
{"trans": "In summary, the factors of uncertainty in the commodity market are endless, and financial hegemony continues to manipulate the market, with the rules of the game changing frequently. Against the backdrop of a global debt crisis and a mixed outlook for the world economy's recovery, the US dollar remains the primary factor influencing the trends of commodities. Economic policies in Europe and the United States have a significant impact, and domestic regulatory measures exacerbate the situation. The interplay of these three factors—financial conditions and market confidence—inevitably leads to significant fluctuations in the commodity market."}
{"trans": "Chinese Red represents a fascinating spiritual and cultural essence that is unique to the Chinese people. It embodies a powerful spirit of perseverance, sincerity, diligence, and kindness, as well as an indomitable spirit. These qualities have been passed down for thousands of years and form the very essence of Chinese culture. Liantianhong, a leading furniture company, passionately promotes the spirit of Chinese Red. With its commitment to integrity as the foundation of its business philosophy, the company has taken the lead in making the production process in its workshops transparent, setting a new standard for the industry and transforming the face of the furniture sector."}
{"trans": "Characteristics: In \"Journey to the West,\" Tang Seng is a tall man with elegant manners and a kind personality. He possesses a profound knowledge of Buddhism. On his journey to the West in search of sacred scriptures, he encounters eighty-one difficulties. Despite these challenges, his devotion never wavers. With the assistance of his disciples Sun Wukong, Zhu Bajie, and Sha Wujing, he endures countless hardships and finally retrieves the true scriptures. Sun Wukong, also known as the \"Pilgrim,\" is Tang Seng's eldest disciple. He possesses fiery golden eyes and can perform seventy-two transformations, as well as ride the clouds and mist. He detests evil and is fearless in the face of difficulties; he is perseverant and valiant."}
{"trans": "III. Attitude towards learning: I have my own set of methods—“developing a sense for solving problems” and “staying up less late.” In fact, once you become proficient through practice, although it may not be possible to solve problems instantly, you at least gain a good understanding of how to approach them. I do not advocate for the “drill-and-kill” approach, as there’s no need to repeatedly work on the same types of problems. Instead, we should compare similar problems and think deeply about them to identify the general methods for solving them. This so-called “sense for solving problems” is similar to the “sense of language” that we often talk about in English learning."}
{"trans": "The longest man-made structure in the world is the Great Wall of China. The magnificent Great Wall stretches across the northern peaks of China, with a total length of over 6,700 kilometers, and its construction began during the Spring and Autumn and Warring States periods. It is a rare example of an ancient military defense project in the history of human architecture, renowned for its long history, massive scale, and impressive grandeur. It has been listed as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO and is hailed as the “Eighth Wonder of the World.”"}
{"trans": "They keep a low profile because they have capital; they remain understated because they stand out from the crowd and cannot conform to common trends. Essentially, luxury goods are exceptional, even unique. They do not allow any compromise in terms of quality or the representation of fashion, and they also possess impeccable superiority in the realms of artistic and stylistic culture. Luxury goods may not be considered necessities of life, but their unparalleled craftsmanship and the rich heritage of their brands certainly make them essential elements in one's existence."}
{"trans": "Although her legs felt as if they were filled with lead, she still strode across the street towards the parking garage. Now, drowsy and alone behind the wheel, she drove along the fluorescently lit concrete lanes, feeling her consciousness blur. Seventeen hours earlier, when she had parked her car here, there were two station wagons on either side of it—so close together that she had to maneuver carefully to get out of the vehicle. Now her old “Taurus” stood alone, like an orphan, in the eighth floor of the parking lot."}
{"trans": "Ten years ago, perhaps no one knew that the internet could be taken with us wherever we went, just as laptops became a common part of our lives. Twenty years earlier, it was unimaginable that phones could be put in our pockets and become an indispensable part of our work and daily activities. Today, a variety of smart devices are exerting an unprecedented influence, subtly changing the way we live. In the next decade, there is a high likelihood of even more groundbreaking innovations in areas such as devices, displays, virtual reality, information sharing, and consumer electronics!"}
{"trans": "We advocate for teamwork and admire the heroism of those who risk their lives to save their comrades. However, we must ensure that we do not become a burden or a hindrance to them. We should try our best to prevent our comrades from taking unnecessary risks in order to rescue us. Strict training and the ability to make quick, informed decisions in critical situations are absolutely essential! Before you’ve experienced the realities of combat, stop showing us your theoretical knowledge and empty talk. There are things that you, as a young officer just out of school, simply don’t understand."}
{"trans": "It’s strange that I haven’t fully understood the five-character poems about the poplar trees and the seven-character poems written by my grandfather. Although I have been gradually improving my skills in the art of “pretending to be confused,” I haven’t achieved a complete understanding of it. Last night, a silent mosquito bit my neck, and I shouted loudly, “How can you bite someone without making a sound? How can you suck blood in such a deceitful way? Why can’t you learn to be a proper mosquito and charge towards my neck with a proper ‘whoosh’?” As a result, I live a tired and absurd life, often hearing the mocking laughter of mosquitoes."}
{"trans": "As barbecue restaurants spring up like mushrooms in every corner of the city, people’s evenings are becoming increasingly enjoyable. However, it’s really difficult to find a place that offers both delicious food and an elegant atmosphere. As the sun sets, painting the sky in shades of red and blending it with the lush green lawns of the sports fields, tables are strategically arranged according to the terrain. Barbecue chefs skillfully prepare the food, servers move around efficiently, and customers enjoy themselves in cheerful conversations. Soft, soothing music plays in the background, creating a truly romantic atmosphere."}
{"trans": "Hearing what I said, the old gentleman let out a long sigh and said, “Oh, I’ve survived so many near-death experiences; it’s really hard to put into words!” Thus, this proud and stubborn old man finally opened up his tumultuous life and inner world to me, a writer he had never met before. As he recounted his stories—sometimes passionately, sometimes solemnly, sometimes with tears streaming down his face, and sometimes with hearty laughter—I witnessed the magnificent yet tragic life of a seventy-year-old man who had endured so much, as well as the power of fate that he could not resist."}
{"trans": "It seems that the Western political arena is far from as clean as people imagine. Beneath the facade of integrity, there lies a beneath-the-table world of corruption and deceit, only with a distinct Western flavor. Politicians stage grand spectacles of “sowing” while secretly “reaping” legitimate gains. Calculating politicians and shrewd capitalists work in tacit agreement, with a mutual understanding. The game of exchanging favors between officials and businessmen, as well as the trade of power for money, is played with such sophistication that it becomes both public and legal—a level of sophistication that even Western democracy and the legal system are powerless to address."}
{"trans": "After wading for several hours, a vast and suddenly open cave came into view. “My god, this isn’t just an underground cave—it’s like an entire underground forest!” one of the team members exclaimed. The cave was as large as a basketball court, with a rugged ground covered in rocks, babbling streams, and crisscrossing ravines. Stalactites as thick as bowls grew over 10 meters high, along with massive stone curtains, uneven rock formations, and intricately intertwined stone pillars—all creating a scene of incredible beauty, reminiscent of a primeval forest. Moreover, the countless crystals shimmered in the light, making it feel like stepping into a fairy-tale world."}
{"trans": "The size of the heart can also be reduced to an incredibly small amount—small enough to accommodate only a home, a person, a sesame seed, or a single virus. A drop of rain can submerge it; a gust of wind can shatter it; a rumor can cause it unbearable pain; a conspiracy can destroy it beyond redemption. The heart can be as hard as any metal known in the world. It can also be as tender as tears, as expressive as silk. It can be extremely resilient, remaining intact despite countless setbacks and humiliations. Yet, it can also be incredibly fragile, instantly shattered with the slightest carelessness."}
{"trans": "Strolling through this place, one is surrounded by shaded trees and a profusion of blossoms in a dazzling array of colors, creating a serene and breathtaking beauty. A gentle breeze carries a refreshing fragrance that instantly lifts one’s spirits. The winding, stone-paved paths are lined with strategically placed plants, and the sound of babbling streams adds to the multi-dimensional landscape, forming a vivid and vibrant tapestry of life. With every step, the view changes: every flower, leaf, blade of grass, tree, and spring reveals its unique charm, drawing one away from the hustle and bustle of the world and allowing one to experience the beauty of harmony between man and nature, a cleansing experience for the soul. Wandering through such picturesque surroundings, one can fully indulge in the joys of this earthly paradise."}
{"trans": "The infuriated former whaler ship said, “This is the whale we caught.” The proud current whaler ship replied, “How come it’s here with us?” The infuriated party said, “It escaped again.” The proud party countered, “Who told you not to tie it securely?”"}
{"trans": "Your pretentious facade cannot hide your arrogance and greed! The hypocritical doctors, the nonsense-spouting witches, and the eloquent swindlers are all mocking our incompetence—be careful of the consequences! You ungrateful husbands, thinking you are so clever and capable. You despise love and kindness…"}
{"trans": "A farce that lasted for two months has finally come to an end. We’re not sure why Foxconn is so angry about these two reports. Such a wealthy and powerful company certainly has access to a team of advisors. In terms of crisis communication tactics, aside from expressing sorrow and tears, they can also choose to demonstrate public anger in a dramatic manner—perhaps as a warning to others, or as a diversion of attention."}
{"trans": "Rewards should be based on merit and performance. Delicious food surely deserves to belong to those who deserve it. “I see you as both pitiful and ridiculous, so arrogant and self-important,” the wild duck replied. “Your views are skewed. We wild ducks fly across the heavens, unbound by any ties, considering the entire world as our home. Yet you depend on others for your survival; we feed ourselves, while you beg for food from others.”"}
{"trans": "The beginning of an article is the most challenging part. It must be abrupt and vigorous, get straight to the point, and hit the mark immediately in order to captivate the reader. There’s no need for beating around the bush or using clichés. He also told me that when reasoning reaches a point where it becomes difficult to understand or distinguish between different ideas, using an analogy can easily resolve all the confusing arguments. How economical and skillful that is!"}
{"trans": "She began to perform the divination in a very serious manner. After a while of busy activity, she pretended to examine the sand tray again, made some calculations, and then looked up at Kudi, saying, “You damned shameless wretch! How dare you talk nonsense in front of me! The divination is clear: your name is Kudi, and you are a thief and murderer who has committed every conceivable evil deed, beyond redemption.”"}
{"trans": "The castle was indeed like a paradise on earth. As he admired the magnificent architecture, his heart was filled with both wonder and envy. They wandered through the gardens, picking fresh fruits to eat, and immersed themselves in the beautiful sounds of birds and the fragrance of flowers, so much so that they wanted to stay forever. By the time they had leisurely explored the entire castle, it was already dark, and they returned to the hall by the pond, deciding to spend the night there."}
{"trans": "The air conditioning is indeed very effective. The cool, fresh air, the well-organized layout, the neatly dressed guests, and the polite staff all contribute to creating a sense of exclusivity and comfort. However, it’s the people who often spoil the experience. Those neatly dressed gentlemen all look so greasy and smug after eating, which is quite unpleasant to watch. They all nodded at Nicholas, and for some reason, some of them even gave him suggestive glances."}
{"trans": "The Japanese began to waver; realizing that they were at their wit’s end and that the situation was hopeless, they finally gave up resistance and fled towards the city. The armored trains continued to move back and forth, sweeping away the remaining enemies. They were like two majestic, roaring dragons on land, unstoppable in their progress, leveling the fortifications where the enemies had hidden and sending those who tried to flee to their doom. This was a resounding victory for the Chinese army, signaling the coming end of the stubborn and unyielding invaders."}
{"trans": "After going through such a calamity, our family never recovered. Our family fortune declined, and we fell into poverty and hardship, struggling to survive in hunger and cold. The old locust tree also lost its former glory; the remaining half of the trunk stood alone, desolate in the half-barren courtyard, exposed to the elements—wind, rain, dew, and frost. For many years, it neither sprouted new leaves nor branches, and no one paid attention to it. It simply stood there, “raising its eyes to the sky and sighing.”"}
{"trans": "Everything reactionary will not fall unless you strike it down. Dust won’t clean itself away just because a broom hasn’t reached it. You all are finished; only I, Zhang Pujing, the loyal Bolshevik, remain pure and upright. The revolution is not about inviting people to dinner, writing articles, painting, or frying dough sticks. The proletariat has brought you all under its dictatorship—these demons and monsters. Haha!"}
{"trans": "Overemphasizing the achievements of top scorers in the college entrance examination can make them feel superior to others. Some may become complacent, arrogant, and self-centered, inadvertently lowering their standards for themselves in future work and life, becoming stagnant and unable to cooperate effectively with others. Others may believe they must always be better than others, striving for perfection and being overly cautious and risk-averse in their actions. Both of these attitudes can lead to a lack of creativity and passion in their endeavors, making it difficult for them to achieve great things."}
{"trans": "I will treat every one of my patients with equal respect, regardless of whether their clothing is luxurious or shabby, whether they are handsome or unattractive, whether they are wealthy or in need, whether their status is high or low, whether they are clean and tidy or covered in scars, whether they suffer from serious illnesses or minor ailments, whether they are polite to me or rude, whether they are well-educated or illiterate, whether they are humorous or dull, whether they are nobles or commoners..."}
{"trans": "Love is free. That involuntary admiration, that unstoppable longing, that deep affection that supports one through thick and thin, that enduring love that cares for each other in times of need—these are the deepest comforts and strongest supports in life. And all of this is free; it cannot be bought with money. Goals are also free. Whether you are a prince living in luxury or a homeless wanderer, as long as you want to, you can set a goal for your life. This goal can be as great or as ordinary as you wish; it can be as splendid or as simple as you desire. As long as you want to, you can achieve it."}
{"trans": "Once you have set your goals, you should concentrate your efforts on planning the path to success and then proceed with all your might. During this time, you must not be distracted or indecisive. You should strictly eliminate doubt and fear, as they can undermine your determination, destroy your enthusiasm for progress, and hinder your actions towards achieving your goals. Those who are filled with doubt and fear will end up achieving nothing. When doubt and fear creep into your mind, your goals, energy, motivation, and all your positive thoughts will be severely impacted and collapse."}
{"trans": "A cultivated person holds a sense of respect, awe, and admiration for the many excellent qualities of humanity, such as loyalty, bravery, trust, diligence, mutual assistance, selflessness in saving others, courage in the face of danger, endurance in hardship, and unwavering integrity. Not everyone may be able to embody these qualities in their own lives, but they understand how to cherish and praise them. It is not wrong for people to feel fear or be lazy; however, they should not disguise these flaws as noble virtues. Nor should they condemn those who do practice these virtues as hypocrites simply because they themselves cannot achieve them. You may kneel in the mud, but you should not spread that mud across the entire world and then seriously claim that everything is filthy."}
{"trans": "This world has beginnings that are quiet and unassuming, others that are grand and spectacular; some begin with caution, some with boldness, some with secrecy, some with hesitation, some with ulterior motives, and yet others with complete honesty. Every stage of life, every event in existence, is approached in different ways by different people. These approaches reflect an individual’s approach to managing their life—whether through their mindset, vision, courage, demeanor, or breadth of mind."}
{"trans": "Generally speaking, the review in the final stage plays a crucial role in completing the entire preparation process. Therefore, we must attach great importance to this final phase of review and avoid making any mistakes that could lead to all our previous efforts being wasted and us missing out on success. Below are some common misconceptions that need to be clarified."}
{"trans": "Currently, the market lacks a clear leader; major sectors are adjusting in turn, and the efforts to stabilize the market are insufficient. It is very difficult for mainstream investors to make decisions, which is why the market is weak. It’s like a frightened bird—any negative news can cause panic and lead to increased selling. Meanwhile, off-market investors are still waiting and watching. Coupled with the fact that the desire to take long positions is not strong before the holiday, market sentiment is even more dispirited."}
{"trans": "The Japanese, who were resisting stubbornly in a desperate attempt to hold on, were already on the brink of collapse. Their barely holding front line was like a warship riddled with holes and leaking from all sides; with this fatal blow, it shattered into pieces just like weathered rock. In fact, preventing the armored train from advancing would not have been difficult—all that was needed was to destroy the railway tracks in advance."}
{"trans": "Fish eyes mixed with pearls: How to distinguish the genuine from the fake? The appreciation and popularity of cultural walnut products are on the rise, and as market prices increase, so do the instances of fraud using high-tech methods. At first, Lao Hu was also deceived, but now, with his extensive experience, he’s much more discerning. He even sleeps with walnuts in his hand at night—almost nothing can trick him anymore. He’s shared a few tips with the readers of the evening newspaper to help them identify genuine products from the fake ones."}
{"trans": "In my life, I’ve experienced much the same as others—both the broad, sunny paths and the narrow, wooden bridges. I’ve traveled along a winding, bumpy road. I must admit that I’ve been lucky; the successes I’ve achieved and the fame I’ve gained don’t always live up to their reputation. On the other hand, I’ve also suffered misfortunes that few people have had to endure. During that infamous “Great Revolution,” I nearly lost my life for speaking out for what I believed in. The physical pain I endured will remain with me for a lifetime."}
{"trans": "Zhuge Liang can be regarded as one of the greatest military strategists in Chinese history. He compared himself to Guan Zhong in Longzhong – what a display of confidence! His prediction of the division of the empire into three parts was incredibly accurate. When he first emerged from obscurity, he faced Xiahou Yu with an army of 100,000 without any fear; the fire attack on Bowang Slope convinced Guan Yu and Zhang Fei of his leadership; the fire at Xinye left Cao Ren in utter despair; his ingenious strategies, including the “three provocations of Zhou Yu,” demonstrated both intelligence and a sense of humor. He remained utterly loyal to Liu Bei and refused to proclaim himself emperor, even though he was given the authority to do so. His composure during the forced implementation of the “Empty City” strategy is truly admirable. However, what touches me the most is the story of “Autumn Wind at Wuzhangyuan.”"}
{"trans": "When the night falls in the mountain village, we hear a series of sharp barks from the dogs, one after another. After midnight, the barking fades away, and the lights in the windows begin to shine one by one, like the white faces of cabbages… The moonlight too seems to be washing its face by the water pipes in the yard…"}
{"trans": "Close-range shots are missed; header attempts in front of the goal go awry for some inexplicable reason; even when playing alone against the defender, the opportunity is not capitalized on… The lack of opportunities to train in domestic leagues has resulted in the national youth team’s poor ability to seize opportunities in the attacking phase, which is a major weakness of the current team."}
{"trans": "However, in a sociological sense, the Israeli and Palestinian parties today are sworn enemies. The reasons for this lie in the estrangement, indifference, suspicion, and hostility that arose over more than 1,000 years, since the Jews fled Palestine in 556 BCE and were scattered around the world, resulting in the separation of two brothers who never met again. Additionally, the return of the Jews to Palestine and the establishment of the State of Israel 2,000 years later has led to mutual strife and the complete disappearance of any sense of kinship or brotherly ties."}
{"trans": "National policies are implemented from above, and the situation within the industry has taken a dramatic turn for the worse. Ceramic production areas have been hit the hardest, resembling beasts trapped in a predicament. These areas are struggling, while ceramic companies are trying to find their way forward. As the cold wave arrives, it brings not only shock and pain to these regions but also a clearer understanding of the path ahead. For more details: The industry situation has deteriorated rapidly, and many ceramic production areas are fighting for survival like beasts in distress."}
{"trans": "Stepping into the Suzhou Gardens and wandering through its courtyards, one may encounter small bridges over flowing streams, pink walls and black-tiled roofs; or take winding paths that lead to secluded spots with surprising turns. The scenery changes with every step, offering endless variety. The most striking aspect is the meticulous craftsmanship displayed in the garden's design, which bears a striking resemblance to the imperial gardens of the Forbidden City. The arrangement of corridors, pavilions, and waterside structures is well-organized and layered, creating an illusion of spaciousness even on narrow paths of just 20 meters wide, giving the sense of walking through a painting."}
{"trans": "The situation on the battlefield is constantly changing, and there has never been a fixed formula for winning battles since ancient times. Decisions regarding the deployment of troops, the choice of tactics (offensive or defensive), the type of warfare (stationary or mobile), whether to abandon certain positions or to defend them, which areas to sacrifice and which to hold onto, etc., should all be made by the frontline commanders themselves. The supreme commander should not interfere too much. In fact, any strategy or tactic can be combined and applied flexibly; it's hard to say which method is necessarily superior. This is what is meant by the saying, \"All roads lead to Rome\"—the only real criterion is winning the battle."}
{"trans": "A novel is like the soul viewed in reverse light; you infuse a part of your own soul into the work, giving it your very essence and thus elevating it to the level of art. This involves two key issues. First, the writer must examine the true state of their own soul and shape themselves before they can shape their creations. Second, the power of sincerity is immense. Here, sincerity is not merely about correcting excesses; it also means rejecting artificiality, pandering, sensationalism, and opportunistic writing practices. Don’t just scratch the surface; don’t engage in absurd or offensive behavior, and certainly don’t sell sincerity as some sort of quick fix. I believe sincerity should be an attitude towards life, especially for a writer."}
{"trans": "The old pagoda tree by the window, weathered by time, remains motionless; the moon, also immobile, hangs from its branches, resembling a bell yet so distant from its actual sound. I know that one shouldn’t expect such trivial things to make a resounding impact upon the ground. Yet it is precisely this moonlight, as insignificant as dust, that makes the silent midnight even more akin to a sunken ship in the middle of the night."}
{"trans": "Heartless and cruel, deceitful and cunning—yet I am kind and generous, striving to bring salvation to all beings. Within the gloomy mansion of Dis, my spirit draws symbols and writings with great concentration. Suddenly, the painful cries of Dorcineia from Toboso reach me, and I learn that she has unfortunately been struck by magic."}
{"trans": "Internet analyst Xu Dandan, who suspects that some companies may act in a way that undermines their own future success, believes that Alibaba exhibits such behavior. “Capital has its own nature, and it is only natural for them to act in the best interests of their shareholders. Taking over an investment means assuming the responsibilities associated with that capital contract. One should not treat capital as a deity when it is needed, but criticize it as a demon when it poses obstacles.”"}
{"trans": "Even the most perceptive gaze is powerless in the face of such circumstances! Our eyes are dazzled, and we dare not look directly at the throne. We come from the East, yet the trouble arose in the West; our ranks are vast and long—so long that we cannot see their end. One after another, we press forward in a rush of courage, armed with spears. We fight one against ten, ten against a hundred… Yet countless lives are lost, and all traces of them vanish without a trace."}
{"trans": "Just as he had successfully obtained the Zhubai Green and was feeling extremely pleased with himself, he had to go on a long journey due to some matter. When he returned home, he learned from the family that the Zhubai Green, along with a bag of gold and silver, had disappeared without a trace. Upon hearing this news, he flew into a rage, shouting and cursing at himself, and even tore his clothes apart. The more he thought about the wasted effort of carrying the bamboo basket to fetch water, the angrier he became."}
{"trans": "2008 was an extraordinary year. On the battlefield of public relations and marketing for domestic companies, it was also a time of intense competition and turmoil. For corporate public relations professionals, it seemed as if “public relations crises” struck overnight, like fierce storms, causing great fear and anxiety. Time flies by, and in the blink of an eye, we are about to step into 2009. Looking back on that year, many business owners may still feel lingering fears, as if walking on thin ice."}
{"trans": "Friends born under the sign of Leo are almost always willing to help with work, as long as they can showcase their talents and abilities. They will do their best to assist others, even if it means putting in extra effort. However, this can sometimes lead to them forgetting things or accumulating a heavy workload. Therefore, a handy calendar and weekly plan are the perfect tools for managing their work efficiently. Especially ones with a lively and childlike style, which align well with their innocent and natural nature, allowing them to handle even the busiest tasks with ease."}
{"trans": "An excellent essay should contain six or seven outstanding sentences: first, vivid and beautiful metaphors; second, majestic parallel sentences; third, emotionally charged personifications; fourth, well-referenced sentences that draw on profound cultural heritage; fifth, thought-provoking philosophical statements; sixth, contrasting sentences that enhance the overall effect; and seventh, poetic sentences that are both expressive and beautiful. By skillfully using these sentences, the writing becomes concise yet meaningful, adding the final touch that illuminates the entire piece, making each sentence effective as if it were ten. This approach naturally enhances the literary quality of the essay."}
{"trans": "What’s even more ridiculous is that, nowadays, the economies of Western countries are still in a difficult situation. The money-printing machines are about to start operating again, but there’s no financial resources left to support them, and yet they still expect China to “feed” the world… Everyone is now turning their attention towards China, the world’s second-largest economy. If the global system established after the Cold War, which was controlled by the United States, is already on the verge of collapse, will this newly emerging economic superpower step forward to save it? Or will it simply let the West suffer the consequences of its own actions? However, this time, China might be unable to do much about it."}
{"trans": "Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, reigned for 54 years and expanded China’s territory. The empire stretched from Liaodong and central Korea in the east to the shores of Lake Balkhash in the west, to the heart of Vietnam in the south, and to the Saiin Mountains in Outer Mongolia in the north, encompassing a vast expanse of land. During his reign, the population reached nearly 60 million. To be fair, among the hundreds of emperors in Chinese history, very few were able to expand the country’s borders as significantly as Emperor Wu of Han. Those who were able to maintain their empire and avoid becoming disgraced rulers who lost national sovereignty were already doing quite well. In this sense alone, Emperor Wu of Han can indeed be considered a great and visionary emperor."}
{"trans": "His short stories often reflect the mundane aspects of ordinary people’s lives, lacking the dramatic twists and turns that one might expect from a more conventional narrative. However, they are refreshing due to their unique perspectives and the unmistakable personal flavor of the author. He has a knack for creating characters with distinctive personalities, a trait that is certainly characteristic of a genius writer."}
{"trans": "Some people put on a showy front, using grand titles and claims to position themselves as the best or first in their industry, constantly promoting themselves in a flood of information. Others, on the other hand, adopt a more cautious approach, preferring to keep their wealth and achievements hidden, to focus on their work quietly without making a fuss."}
{"trans": "In fact, why do these “verbal battles” always seem to be overwhelming and persist for months without ceasing? What forces are behind them, fueling the intensity of the arguments? And what exactly is influencing the judgments and thoughts of internet users? Not only ordinary netizens but also some website administrators are deeply confused by this phenomenon."}
{"trans": "That evening, he laid out the manuscript paper and prepared to write an article in order to earn back those 20 yuan. The title of his article that night was “On the Necessity and Possibility of Morality.” He wrote: “In an era dominated by degenerate materialism, we must raise the banner of morality and fight against the enslavement of the human spirit by material possessions.” His essay was filled with passionate and vehement expressions of indignation, moral indignation, and a deep desire to guide others towards goodness. It was a piece of writing that was passionate, eloquent, and flowed smoothly, conveying a powerful message that resonated with the reader."}
{"trans": "1. In the examination of essay writing, one must have a far-reaching perspective. As an official document, the most fundamental characteristic of an essay is that its purpose and theme should be of a high caliber. When writing such essays, one should consider the long-term interests, see through the surface to the essence, and be adept at providing a comprehensive and insightful analysis as well as elevating the theme. In other words, the resulting articles should embody a noble intellectual realm; they must not be vulgar, nor should they be lowbrow or filled with complaints."}
{"trans": "He is often melancholic, but his melancholy is a manifestation of compassion for those who suffer. When he smiles, his smile is like the longing of people seeking the unknown, like the dust of stars falling before the eyes of children, and like a piece of bread in his throat."}
{"trans": "If you look even higher, how exquisitely shaped her shoulders are! They resemble twin lambs or two peaks of jade; as slender as the mountains in autumn and as smooth as the waters in autumn. Above her shoulders lies the face that is the subject of so much praise and admiration from people."}
{"trans": "Even the lotus plant suffers the tragedy of having its entire family exterminated. The lotus petals are connected to each other; their “thousands of fingers” hold onto a summer, only to let it go again. Now, it’s the ghostly rain of autumn nights, pouring down on the surface of the broken duckweed, like a disheveled, blind Chopin tormenting a piano with a thousand keys."}
{"trans": "Listening to Zen under the moonlight enhances one’s understanding; discussing swordsmanship under the moonlight makes one’s words more sincere; discussing poetry under the moonlight adds a touch of elegance; and encountering a beautiful person under the moonlight deepens one’s feelings. The proper way to appreciate the moon is as follows: when it is bright and clear, one should look up at it; when it is hazy, one should look down at it. The spring breeze is like wine; the summer breeze is like tea; the autumn breeze is like smoke; the winter breeze is like the scent of ginger and mustard."}
{"trans": "He rode the waves of blood, aboard a small red boat, and gracefully arrived in this damp and cold world. His final leap was propelled out of the gates of life by the surging heatwaves, just like the mud and sand being carried away by a flood. The baby’s intense cries sounded like glass cups shattering against each other."}
{"trans": "If China has one more gloomy writer, this north-facing study should bear the responsibility for that. Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a fruit from the south, fully ripe and now stored in the refrigerator. By day, I seem to be immersed in the depths of the ocean, where a silent, gloomy atmosphere plays a grayish melody."}
{"trans": "The red candle possesses a kind of spirituality; it does not begrudge its life, yet it cherishes it especially. Whenever it is about to burn out, the charred wick seems to arch high and spasmatically, like a spine, amidst the flames. It holds its ground, resembling a warrior suddenly struck by a bullet who freezes in mid-air into an indomitable statue, only to then collapse back into the pool of glowing red liquid…"}
{"trans": "When you go outside and look up at the sky, you can see that it has its own “latitude and longitude” (a way of organizing its structure). After the morning dew or rain, the sun emerges, and the sky is covered with tiny, glittering particles that shine brightly together, as if one sun has given birth to countless others. There’s no need to sweep the old net in the corner of the wall; let the dust accumulate on it. Over time, the ropes of the net become thick, just like the roots of an old tree. This net can serve as a three-dimensional mural, offering a reflection of both tradition and modernity—a source of constant inspiration that never becomes outdated."}
{"trans": "Spring is always the first to knock on the bamboo gate of the garden, and then it lights the torches that were extinguished last year, one by one. At this moment, winter, which dwells alone in the empty houses, is like a howling wolf that flees in the sudden burst of flames. The flames leave its lonely gaze at a loss, and the flowers on the earth make it lose its way."}
{"trans": "The means of punishing evil are even more evil than evil itself; indiscriminate killing of the innocent is as effortless as cutting down grass. Under the banner of loyalty, filial piety, integrity, and righteousness, there is only the clashing of swords and the glint of blades. The price of such grandeur is a landscape littered with corpses. The basic value of life is reduced to mere blades of withered grass trampled under horse hooves; the right to exist of the common people is likened to mere bubbles on the edge of a whirlpool."}
{"trans": "—the sounds of heaven, the mysteries of infinity, the imprisonment of the finite by the infinite, or the stern yet gentle commands of God. Music is the all-knowing, all-powerful God of musical notes; He is both the Creator who arranges and determines the positions of these notes and the Savior who awaits those notes to listen attentively and follow the never-ending melody."}
{"trans": "Over the winding lotus pond, one can see a dense expanse of leaves. The leaves emerge from the water quite high, resembling the skirts of graceful dancers. interspersed among the layers of leaves are scattered white flowers—some blooming gracefully, others still in their shy bud stage. They are like precious pearls, like stars in the blue sky, and also like beautiful women just out of the bath."}
{"trans": "Therefore, in the case of a city, if everything one encounters and sees is young and vibrant, then it is certain that the right balance has not yet been achieved, and the various elements (like the strings of a musical instrument) are not in harmony. This is similar to writing: when adjectives describe a beautifully dressed young woman or parallel sentences depict lovers standing side by side, it means the writer has not yet found the true essence of writing. The pinnacle of writing lies in the beauty of an old street with sparse phoenix trees, an old seat under those trees, and the casual conversations that take place there—elegance combined with a sense of leisure."}
{"trans": "The pain of individual families does not affect the happiness of the world. Summer arrives irresistibly; the acacia flowers, like pink powders, brush against the lonely and desolate windows of the hospital rooms. The girl’s head has taken on a polygonal shape; the long-healed fractures in her bones resemble cracked earth, creating black holes beneath her thin skin, as some inner evil force expands in all directions."}
{"trans": "Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a fruit, ripe with the essence of the south, refrigerated inside a freezer. By day, I seem to be immersed in the depths of the ocean, where a silent, gloomy atmosphere plays a grayish melody. At night, I can almost hear the sound of Inuit sleds gliding across the snow; the long beard of the North Star hangs down, clanging against the clusters of white stalactites."}
{"trans": "They were as quiet as the bright moon, not wishing to disturb anyone, yet they indeed caused a great stir in the surrounding area. This can truly be described as “the moon rising, startling the birds in the mountains.” Compared to Tao Yuanming’s tranquility, Wang Wei’s tranquility has a more aristocratic air and a sense of exquisite craftsmanship. His brilliance lies in his ability to be more “commoner” than the commoners and his designs to be more “natural” than nature itself."}
{"trans": "Even that brown coffee table is depicted with great emotion; it’s a gentle, elongated rectangle that bears all the hustle and bustle happening on it. There’s also a larger table, adorned with white magnolias that are thin and shiny, resembling both jade and crystal, and evoking the coolness of a jade fish that Yang Guini holds in her mouth when her baby tooth hurts. The strong, resilient lines of the winter jasmine flowers open and close with determination; its control over life is both graceful and assertive."}
{"trans": "“Vast and boundless… I shall return to that great wilderness!” When I read this passage, it doesn’t evoke sadness in me; rather, it fills me with beauty. It’s like reading the “Records of the Grand Historian” and encountering the story of Jing Ke, who, dressed in white, crossed the Yi River to assassinate the King of Qin—full of vivid imagery and emotion. Imagine a young man from a wealthy family who has seen through the ways of the world, standing bareheaded and barefoot in a red cloak on the snowy ground, bidding farewell to his father… How beautiful that must be!"}
{"trans": "We cannot transcend that dark, humiliating, and indifferent era of Chengde, just as we cannot avoid facing the ugly and desolate Taoist Pagoda when approaching the Mogao Caves. No matter how splendid and magnificent the memories of Dunhuang may be, they cannot fill the vastness of the scripture caves, nor can they erase the pallor within the Thousand Buddha Caves, nor can they heal the wounds of an ancient nation that has shed blood on the horizon."}
{"trans": "Forgetting increasingly often visits us and becomes a friend that lasts until the end of our lives. I use this “friend” to make selections: what has been forgotten doesn’t need to be remembered. The subconscious manipulates our memories, just as the wind directs a kite on an invisible level. New, complex patterns are woven into a web of uneven memory; what remains is like cheese—sweet, yet containing hard, sharp chunks that can be irritating to the teeth."}
{"trans": "His chest is massive and upright, embodying the thunderous roars of his ancestors as they chased fierce beasts through the wilderness. The pelvis is deeply indented, with sharply protruding bones indicating the presence of once-strong muscle groups that, like the ropes used by the laborers along the Yellow River, enabled his body to climb with the agility of a gecko. His limbs, resembling the long, beautiful ivory tusks of African elephants, emit a lustrous sheen as smooth as congealed fat."}
{"trans": "It took several years for me to let go of my resentment and to acknowledge that that day was a crucial turning point in my life. What prompted me to destroy that painting of the withered rose was not the mockery of my art teacher, but rather the sheer brilliance of your talent—so dazzling that I broke my paintbrush myself, with a gesture full of regret. What is regret like? It’s like a small mole on one’s body; only one knows its exact location and the process by which it appeared."}
{"trans": "I was combing my hair on the balcony, and my hair fell out just like fallen leaves, in strands that brushed against my arms, like the rain at night. From far and near, the car horns sounded in a panic; the sky gradually darkened, and the lake stretched out in all directions, like a vast expanse of mist and rosy clouds. From a window on the lowest floor of the house across from me, a wisp of pale white smoke rose hesitantly into the air, as if not quite knowing where the sky was."}
{"trans": "She was carrying a kettle in each hand, which reminded me of the woman walking with energy along a thin rope. It was all due to her waist; her waist was so flexible that, in plain terms, it was so soft that it made me feel as if I were eating Suzhou-style gelatin. Not only her waist, but as my diary states: she possesses curves that can rival the beauty of clouds and the charm of the moon and water, weaving a vast, deceptive web!"}
{"trans": "“Because of your language, you remain silent; when you sink to the deepest depths, you make yourself disappear.” By losing your language, you lose your self, the essence of your existence. Yang Lian thus realizes that he has become a “ghost.” A ghost, drifting between cities, watching with cold eyes (just like an insect, a ghost is also a ‘it’ that can only observe), witnessing the complete disappearance of something called “meaning.” There is a sea, but the port holds no meaning for you."}
{"trans": "One lamp is situated far from another streetlight; between segments of brightness, there are stretches of darkness. My shadow appears sometimes in the light and sometimes vanishes into the darkness. The wind, coming out of nowhere, ripples through the colorful fallen leaves, as if stirring up the impressions of life itself. I feel like I am this empty wind, capable of capturing my own existence only when the leaves fall and are swirlled up in the air."}
{"trans": "But we, standing on that open piece of land—my father, my brother, my relatives, and many fellow villagers who had toiled, sweated, been scorched by the sun, and braved the elements—just stood there, listening to the distant thunder, with no one showing the slightest desire to take shelter from the rain coming from the northwest. Our hearts were heavier than the dryness of the sky itself; everyone was silent, for our hearts were also like the rainy sky, and this “rain of hearts” seemed even more solemn and relentless than the rain from the northwest."}
{"trans": "Imagine if both Tang Bohu and Qianlong had become “first-rate poets of ancient China”; then we would have had no choice but to quietly burn the entire collection of “The Complete Tang Poems.” The same is true for calligraphy: an astonishingly high price paid for a work of mediocre quality is like a pile of gold weighing down the scales of Chinese calligraphy history. Faced with this situation, I once sighed deeply: “When the cultural heritage is hidden, a small hill is considered a mountain; when the strong wings have flown far away, mere remnants are enough to symbolize a giant bird like the roc.”"}
{"trans": "The episodes occurred suddenly, as if the girl had received some divine command from the heavens; there were no warning signs before the sudden spasms began. The once soft and delicate girl contracted into a figure resembling a rigid dough roller, with every muscle shining like iron. Her small body acted like a bent bow from which an arrow could be shot; she bounced on the pale, snow-white hospital bed. Countless beads of sweat dripped down from this bizarre “human rainbow,” similar to the snow melting from the eaves during the warmth of spring."}
{"trans": "The power that is released is solitary yet powerful; it follows rules yet also breaks them. It is imbued with a sense of intoxication and poetry, akin to the Dionysian spirit described by Nietzsche. With this Dionysian spirit, Zhang Xu used his writing brush as if it were a drunken, staggering step—swaying and dancing, with a graceful posture and full of energy, he executed all his movements in one fluid motion. Then he would throw his cup aside and laugh, falling into a deep sleep. Zhang Xu did not realize that his drunken gait was also the very essence of the culture of the Tang Dynasty."}
{"trans": "But just as I was holding my breath and listening intently, suddenly, everyone stopped talking at the same time. That cicada gave me another shock! It was as if a rope had tightly bound my heart with its sound, and then, without any warning, that rope was released. My heart, unprepared, scattered like a wave that leaps towards the sky but accidentally falls onto the beach! I don’t even know when summer has already crossed the threshold and come upon us…"}
{"trans": "I have wept in sadness for your humiliations and disappointments. My tears flowed like streams, clear as crystal, yet they could not wash away the deep stains on you; they only removed the obstructions from my eyes. These tears could not moisten your hearts of stone; instead, they only extinguished the flames of anxiety and fervor within me. Now, in response to your suffering, I laugh—a laugh as thunderous as the roar of a storm. It does not come after the storm, but before it."}
{"trans": "I gradually came to understand that when facing disasters, we cannot use the “grammar of disaster”; there is another kind of grammar that leads us directly to a poetic realm of spiritual freedom. From that moment on, my state of being was never the same. Every time I read Zhuangzi’s works such as “Autumn Waters,” “Free and Easy Wandering,” “On the Equality of Things,” and “The World,” it was as if I were looking at electrocardiograms that were closely related to me. It is difficult for me to provide a calm and impartial assessment of such a profoundly intimate ancient philosopher; therefore, I can only choose to avoid discussing him."}
{"trans": "You press your forehead against the embroidered patterns covered with gold thread. When the sun is on this side, it heats the gold threads until they become scorching hot; yet now it’s cold. The efforts of the people from long ago have gradually faded into obscurity, their deeds covered in dust. When their descendants hang out their clothes, they shake off that dust, which then dances in the yellow sunlight. If these memories had a scent, it would be the fragrance of camphor—sweet and comforting, like a joy that remains vivid in the mind, or like a sorrow that has been forgotten."}
{"trans": "It is precisely to this extent that they have become close to us in life, allowing us to connect with them even after thousands of years have passed. The vibrancy of Yang Guifei can be likened to a ceramic teapot, as gentle and smooth as jade. As the water inside gradually cools, it exudes a tender, persistent warmth. Su Qing, on the other hand, is like a small red-clay stove with its own independent flame; one can see the glowing red flames and hear the crackling sounds as the clay peels off. However, she is more demanding to care for—adding coal and wood can be troublesome, and the smoke can be quite irritating to breathe."}
{"trans": "Just like the roaring waves or the terrifying tempests, they strike against the emotions that have settled deep within you. In an instant, you feel as if the chirping of the cicadas, like fierce waves washing away sand, has swept away the slight sorrow you were clutching onto so tightly. The cicadas’ rapid chirping suddenly comes to an abrupt halt at the highest pitch, much like a magnificent piece of writing being violently torn apart, its resounding words scattered across the ground with a sound like that of metal and stone hitting the ground. Then, all that remains is a desolate and incomplete fragment, leaving behind only a sense of melancholy and sadness. Isn’t this also a song of life?"}
{"trans": "Here, there is vibrant youth, and hearts filled with passion and enthusiasm; there are no listless, elderly people, only strong and vigorous young adults. The silvery moon wanders alone in the empty sky, as if in tears, hating its own solitude… And then there’s that swimming pool, always like a kind-hearted old woman with a face full of wrinkles, smiling. When she sees many lively children diving into the water like little mermaids, she bursts into joy, creating huge, silvery splashes."}
{"trans": "For thousands of years, this has been a desolate wasteland lost to history. Beyond the wasteland lie the vague figures of unknown, great craftsmen; on this side of the wasteland stands a terrified contemporary woman. The kilns on both sides burn fiercely, like two beacons separated by mountains and rivers, yet the signals they transmit are precise and unmistakable. While many other beacons are associated with war, these two are not. Amidst the bloodshed of the Three Kingdoms period, the battles of the Sui and Tang dynasties, and the conflicts of the Song, Yuan, Ming, and Qing dynasties, only these two emit wisps of the purest smoke, echoing each other from afar."}
{"trans": "The fragmentation of Lin Daiyu lies in her deeply unforgettable love; the fragmentation of San Mao stems from a moment of clarity and transcendence after experiencing numerous hardships; the fragmentation of Van Gogh is caused by the sun, which uses its golden blade to inflict relentless pain upon him in the light; the fragmentation of Beethoven, on the other hand, is the tragic and magnificent symphony of life, orchestrated by the clash of the supremely spiritual black and white keys. If the fragmentation of those ordinary individuals reveals the purest and most beautiful aspects of human nature, then the fragmentation of these exceptional souls is like silver flowers of gratitude that bloom across the sky above us."}
{"trans": "You wash your face several times a day, yet it still doesn’t seem clean; however, if you never wash your eyes, they will always remain bright. The unused spaces in a room can’t be utilized for the purposes of mops or brooms, so there’s no need to spend money on them. After all, humans are mobile beings, naturally designed to avoid dust. Strangely enough, the air doesn’t become thinner due to the limited space. To better observe a person’s breathing, cigarettes are used as a tangible representation of air: you inhale once, exhale three times, and the smoke rises slowly towards the ceiling. With the auspicious clouds surrounding you, you can first appreciate the diversity of things below, and then look up at the vastness of the universe."}
{"trans": "To know oneself without first knowing others is merely to gather in a small corner and live out one's life without interacting with others; it’s like the insects of summer that cannot speak to the ice, the frogs at the bottom of a well, or the donkeys in the mill. Only by being able to understand others can one truly possess self-awareness. Just like the fan of Princess Iron Fan—one must be able to open it and close it accordingly. The more one knows, the broader one’s connections become. By dispersing oneself throughout the world and immersing oneself in all things, observing their size, shape, weight, and density, one can gradually discern one’s true nature."}
{"trans": "The song is like drifting clouds and flowing water, soothing one’s worries and allowing one to wander within its embrace. Yet it is also like roaring waves and fierce tempests, striking at the emotions buried deep within one’s heart. In an instant, one feels as if the chirping of the cicadas, like turbulent waves washing away sand, has swept away the gentle sorrows that one clutched tightly. The sudden halt in the cicadas’ rapid song, at the highest pitch, is akin to a splendid piece of literature being violently torn apart, its vibrant words scattered across the ground with a resonant clatter, like the sound of metal and stone hitting the ground. Afterwards, all that remains is a desolate and incomplete fragment, leaving behind only a sense of melancholy and sadness."}
{"trans": "What is there of nothingness? The affairs of God are unknown to man; the affairs of man, on the other hand, are about constructing and continuing meaning within the confines of fate—perhaps even out of helplessness—thereby saving both the present and eternity. Therefore, the “return of eternity” is by no means a “complete affirmation of life on earth,” but rather simply a recognition that man cannot escape life on earth, not even death can do so. As for affirmation, it refers to the pursuit and transcendence towards eternity, the earth’s gaze towards the heavens—a magnificent music that has always filled the sky and the earth."}
{"trans": "Viewing the Zen paintings by Master Xiaoyun brings a completely different experience. It’s as if we’re reading the pastoral poems of Tao Yuanming and Wang Wei in the dead of night. With just a few strokes and a light application of ink, these paintings fail to stir intense emotions in our hearts; instead, they calm our tumultuous feelings. They don’t force something upon us; rather, they cleanse the mundane thoughts that already fill our minds. It’s like a mountain stream after a heavy rain. At first, the water is murky, but as the sky clears after the rain, the stream becomes completely clear, and all the mud and filth in the mountains are washed away."}
{"trans": "The sound varies in speed, pitch, volume, and continuity; at times it’s like the ringing of golden bells or the resonant sound of great chimes; other times it resembles the dropping of large and small pearls onto a jade plate; sometimes it’s like red coral and white shells sinking into the sea; at other times it’s like the playing of a simple zither; yet again, it’s like the thunder of a dancing storm or the chorus of a hundred birds. My thoughts wander freely, and I can’t control them. My heart blooms with joy, and inspiration flows from my pen. The seemingly lifeless words seem to come to life, and I feel as if I’ve been filled with the vitality of youth once more. I rarely experience such a state of mind in my life, and it’s even more difficult to describe to others."}
{"trans": "Perhaps clouds are simply meant to drift in the sky, unlike the sun, which has “wheels of fire” beneath it that allow it to descend to earth to receive my heartfelt greetings and kindness. It’s just an illusion of mine… Yet, that illusion is incredibly beautiful. If the blue sky were a book without words, the clouds would be the silent annotations; and the rapid tracks left by my car on the road would translate the language of the clouds into the latest interpretations of that book. The sky weaves its story with its ever-changing hues of blue, and the clouds use a pure, minimalist style to depict it, all for my eyes to “print” and understand. Together, we are telling the story of Kuafu."}
{"trans": "It was inconvenient for me to take it out and eat it on the plane. When I got back to the United States and tried it, the flavor was too oily and the spiciness was way too intense—it wasn’t at all like the sausage rolls that I occasionally eat from my father’s shop. Next to our house in Shanghai was the Qilin Coffee Shop, which had recently moved there from Tianjin during the war. Every dawn, they would start making bread, and the aroma would trigger a “sensory alarm” of sorts. A rich, fragrant scent would fill the air, powerful and overwhelming, like the most gentle form of an alarm clock… only unfortunately, it would go off at the wrong time, waking people up needlessly, just like the annoying beauty of spring that leaves one feeling helpless. Having such a “fragrant” neighbor was indeed a nuisance."}
{"trans": "Happiness in life is like a piece of sugar used to tempt children to take their medicine, or even more like an electric rabbit that stimulates dogs to race in a dog track. A few minutes or days of happiness make up for a lifetime of suffering we endure. We hope it will come, we hope it will stay, we hope it will come again—these three wishes encapsulate the entire history of human endeavor. While we pursue and wait, time slips by unnoticed. Perhaps we are merely pawns in the game of time, living our lives merely to serve as sacrifices for those years, never truly considering the concept of happiness."}
{"trans": "There is a type of dark silk fabric that exudes a sense of greenery; large black shadows seem to sweep across it, imbued with the energy of wind and thunder. Another type is a Japanese silk material with a light lake hue that displays patterns of wood and water. Every so often, on the fabric, there appear two plum blossoms the size of tea bowls, depicted with iron strokes and silver outlines, reminiscent of the colorful stained glass windows in medieval chapels—where the red glass is framed by heavy iron edges. The most common fabrics found in the market are those whose names are impossible to pronounce; they are neither truly green, gray, nor yellow, and are merely used as backgrounds. These are what are known as neutral colors, also referred to as protective colors, civilized colors, or mixed colors."}
{"trans": "This is all derived from her movements: every step she takes, every stretch of her back, every flick of her hair, every glance she casts, every bow of her head, even the slight fluttering of her garments and the gentle swaying of her skirt—everything is like the flow of honey, the ripple of the wind. How can we not be delighted and in awe? The most adorable part is her delicate waist; in the past, people described willow trees swaying in the wind, and in “Dream of the Red Chamber,” there’s mention of Qingwen’s “water snake waist”—both referring to the suppleness and grace of the waist. But the waist that I adore is truly like the sugar candy from Suzhou, leaving my tongue sweet and my teeth feeling soft. With such a soft waist, her hands and feet naturally possess an elegant and extraordinary grace."}
{"trans": "Some wine bottles were leaning crookedly beside them; not much wine was left in them anymore. It’s a pity I don’t drink alcohol, otherwise, at a time like this, taking a few sips would have been an exquisite pleasure. “I raise my cup to invite the bright moon,” and the moon would shyly slip into your glass. A gentle breeze would blow by, and you could hear the trees on both sides of the mountains rustling. As the branches swayed, the lights would flicker on and off, as if mischievous children were playing hide-and-seek with you. This would complement the sparkling reflections on the river surface, creating a harmonious scene as if they were performing a beautiful melody together. What a wonderful earthly dream this is…"}
{"trans": "I can no longer explain it clearly. With the real sun shining on the stage, how could such a sense of desolation arise? There’s a place where art and reality overlap, creating a hazy effect; it’s as if holding a match and burning it in the sunlight—difficult to see the faint orange-yellow flame, but one can more distinctly feel that one’s own hand is also a temporary existence in that light… The maid on stage sang for a while, carrying a tea tray. With movements reminiscent of a gentle breeze parting flowers and willows, she walked through rooms and over countless thresholds, eventually arriving in the study. She bowed to the young master and held the tea tray high above her eyebrows."}
{"trans": "I saw a tabby cat lying lazily against a crumbling, abandoned wall; morning glories bloomed in a riot of deep greens and vibrant purples. The cat yawned nonchalantly. In the hazy night, the streetlights cast the shadows of the power transformers on the white wall of a construction site, intertwining with the swaying branches of the trees, creating an atmosphere that resembled the balcony where Romeo whispered love songs to Juliet. I also saw the face of the poet Zhou Mengdie; as I waved goodbye to him, his face appeared framed by the small window of a passing bus, as if the entire bus was serving as a grand frame for his portrait."}
{"trans": "You think of that innocent, childlike heart—bare of all pretense, yet full of desire and love for everything—that seems to be lurking in the misty morning fog. No matter how you try to call it back to you, it just won’t return. How profound is this sense of loss… Thus, Mr. Pingbo feels a suffocating loneliness. He speaks to you in a gentle, low voice, like the spring breeze whispering among the green trees, sharing with you the memories of his “childhood” that are both dear and elusive to grasp. Although he can’t stay forever in that “childhood,” if he could invite a few companions to join him on those nostalgic journeys, perhaps the sense of emptiness and melancholy wouldn’t linger on his tongue forever."}
{"trans": "You could also say that it marks the starting point for the Chinese people’s journey towards modernity. However, which other nation has made its transition to modernity in such a hasty, frantic, self-doubting, and disorganized manner as Shanghai? You might describe it as an urban civilization that emerged in opposition to agricultural traditions; yet, which other urban civilization has always been under the constant threat, decomposition, encirclement, and influence of the vast rural forces? In short, it’s a tremendous paradox. When you focus on its negative aspects, it emits a dazzling light; but when you worship its greatness, it turns around to show you its scarred, damaged interior."}
{"trans": "However, the truth is just the opposite. I sat there quietly, listening to the sound of the raindrops falling above my head. In that moment, the sound was more pleasing than silence, and I felt an immense joy within me, as if I had drunk nectar from immortals or inhaled the essence of enlightenment. The sound varied in speed, pitch, and intensity; it was sometimes like the ringing of golden bells and jade chimes, sometimes like large and small pearls falling onto a jade plate, sometimes like red coral and white shells sinking into the sea, sometimes like the playing of a plain zither, sometimes like the thunder of a dancing storm, sometimes like the chirping of a hundred birds, and sometimes like a rabbit startled by a falcon. My thoughts wandered freely, my heart blossomed with delight, and inspiration flowed from my pen."}
{"trans": "There were numerous advertising boards and shops surrounding him, with car horns honking incessantly. He was like the person from the ancient legends who had a dream about yellow millet; however, he had only slept for a short while and didn’t experience such a dream—not to mention that he felt a sense of pity… The Taoist priest walked up to a hardware store, then bowed down, but of course, the store owner didn’t have any money to give him. Ignoring everyone else, the priest simply kowtowed once and then got up. He then started knocking on the door of the cigarette paper shop next door, before “kneeling down in the dust on the ground,” his head hanging low. His movements were like a dark current of water, resembling a black chrysanthemum slowly blooming."}
{"trans": "So what’s the big deal? Birds sing in spring, crickets chirp in autumn, mosquitoes make a “thundering” sound in summer; at night, insects are active while birds rest. Wind and rain don’t happen every day, and dogs don’t bark when no one is around, nor do hens lay eggs without a signal. Only humans produce sounds—through speech, gestures, or machinery, at any time and place. Even when alone in a room with no one to respond to, one can turn on a record player, listen to the radio, or even breathe noisily (like thunder) while sleeping. Language is, of course, a form of sound, but in unpleasant, unwanted, or faintly heard language (be it due to walls or distance), words lose their clarity and distinctiveness, becoming a chaotic mix of sounds that are just as meaningless as the crowing of chickens or the barking of dogs."}
{"trans": "As time passes, the past forever becomes a thing of the past, and it is impossible to return to the moment when two people first met under the blossoming peach trees. However, in human memory, the charm or lingering pain of the past often resurges, extending the present into a continuation of that past charm or pain, even further and more profoundly. If life were a blank book with the pages already bound and numbered, the disturbances caused by past events would be like using too much force when writing a page, causing the ink to seep through to the subsequent pages, leaving an indelible mark. Of course, there is no need to destroy the old pages just for the sake of relief; just as the Yellow Crane has flown away, there is no point in destroying the Yellow Crane Tower. Nevertheless, it is necessary to open the old history under the light of the lamp, to proceed where it is appropriate, and to stop where it is due."}
{"trans": "The far northwest is a barren landscape of basaltic mountains, devoid of any vegetation, and vast deserts where lone smoke rises straight into the sky. As a geologist, you carry a large geological field kit made of canvas on your shoulder; you have been traveling for twenty years. For twenty years, your tent has been like a small boat amidst the sand dunes and seas of sand, illuminated by the cold, crescent moon. The sound of the bells from Hanshan Temple outside Suzhou City… can it reach the passenger ship in the middle of the night? Your wife, that beautiful and delicate lady, is watching you with longing in her eyes; her face is covered with the traces of her yearning. She is trying to retrieve that heart of love that has drifted away. You return home once a year and plant a clump of bamboo in front of the door each time, but then you leave again, leaving her with only the shape of the character “个” (a Chinese character representing “one”) formed by the bamboo leaves."}
{"trans": "If life were a blank book that has already been bound and numbered, the disturbances caused by past events would be like the marks made by a heavy pen while writing a page—these marks would seep through to the subsequent pages and could never be erased. Of course, there’s no need to destroy the old pages just for the sake of relief; just as the Yellow Crane has flown away, there’s no point in destroying the Yellow Crane Tower. However, it is necessary to open the pages of our past history under the light of understanding, to proceed where it’s appropriate and to stop where it’s due. After embracing life in its entirety, we can view both old and new things with greater tolerance, giving them their rightful place and meaning. If it was a beautiful experience, we can see what new branches may grow from that seed; if it was a painful one, we can also observe how a tender sprout emerges from the gloom and reaches into the sunshine."}
{"trans": "Everything seems distant from me; even my own shadow in the bright moonlight appears as blurred as smoke. Just as I was about to turn around and go to sleep, for some reason my steps hesitated for a moment. As a result, the lingering dream of an arrow suddenly came to a halt, only to swiftly continue on its course again, as if it had been shot from a bow."}
{"trans": "What remains in the final hope is merely a form of aesthetic support. Just as a sunken ship in the icy sea is utterly beyond rescue, one looks up at the scene of dark clouds rolling by; just as there is no chance of survival under a onslaught of blades, one looks down at the traces of blood sprayed everywhere. Aesthetic support is the last form of support left."}
{"trans": "What we have gathered from the past and the future are but seeds. When you are wandering amidst the mist, a wish within me wanders there as well. We seek each other out, and from our desires grow dreams—dreams that are endless and boundless."}
{"trans": "In such purity, the dish is oneself, the person who prepares the dish is oneself, and the person who eats the dish is also oneself. Just as love is oneself, the one who knows this love is oneself, and the one who recalls this love is also oneself. One sips this love bit by bit, and through the cup of time, one intoxicates oneself."}
{"trans": "The long pants fit tightly, making it impossible to lift one’s feet. My heart is as pure as a piece of paper, as blank as a newborn baby. I say goodbye to the sea, and to the lone seabird circling in the sky. I will return to speak of the dust of the vast expanse of the world. I pick up my umbrella and my shoes, and I pick up all the aspects of human life."}
{"trans": "It’s impossible to predict. All I hope is that, even if it’s considered a flaw of human nature, it should at least be presented in a proper and respectable manner. It should be like the frown and sigh of a noble warrior, rather than the chaotic brawl of a group of poorly dressed soldiers at night; it should be like the thousand-year-old confrontation of two snow-capped peaks, rather than a bunch of tangled vines around a tree trunk."}
{"trans": "That night, the plateau was incredibly beautiful. The sky resembled a blue magical artifact that had been forged during the Jingtai era of the Ming Dynasty—deep and boundless. Even through the huge, silvery moon, one could still see the metallic blue light behind it. The moonlight couldn’t compete with the tint of the blue sky; it faded away, wispy and faint, like diluted ink."}
{"trans": "Watching the same movie over and over again is like regurgitating the food you’ve already eaten and chewing it again. For that brief moment, the sky above us turns golden, as if covered with wheat straw. I remember someone in Gorky’s book saying that lovers from their youth should not meet again later in life; it’s like a skeleton rising from the ground…"}
{"trans": "As soon as I close my eyes, I think of it; as soon as I open them, I want it again. And when all of this comes rushing at me, almost overwhelming me, I simply don’t know what I really want anymore. I only feel a heart that aches intensely, as if it’s being tightly squeezed by threads of silk, scorched by drops of candle wax, and tossed about on the vast expanse of the sea."}
{"trans": "The echo of your slightest sob will become part of it. “After life is veiled, it is just as hidden and concealed as your greatest souls. When life speaks, all the winds turn into words; when life speaks again, the smile on your lips and the tears in your eyes will also turn into words.”"}
{"trans": "As a result, the collective cultural personality has gradually faded. As spring turns to autumn, the plum blossoms wither and the cranes grow old; culture has become a purposeless waste. An inward-directed pursuit of moral perfection has led to overall immorality. The progress of civilization has thus been halted, leaving behind only a pile of plum petals and crane feathers—like bookmarks—sandwiched between the pages of the nation’s spiritual history."}
{"trans": "To grant a pass to religious spirit based on the standards of science and philosophy is tantamount to engaging in love with the use of intellect and speculation alone; this would surely suppress the passions of life and drain the allure of love. Replacing religious spirit with political and economic policies is akin to considering social status and wealth as conditions for marriage, treating children as mere breeding machines, and thus castrating them spiritually."}
{"trans": "In fact, all the destruction is tangible; all the grievances are difficult to express. Therefore, those answers are also questionable. What is unquestionable, however, are the consequences: the withered grass and broken tiles, which bear the marks of disasters that have occurred throughout history. I am willing to face all of this in a dangerous situation without any protective measures, just as I would remove my gloves to touch the scars on an elderly person’s body."}
{"trans": "Now, I have written so many pages. I see myself like a child copying a passage from a long hymn; the hymn that the angels sang when God created the first man. Perhaps I am like an illiterate person memorizing a sentence from a book written by wisdom, a book that was inscribed on the pages of emotions before time even existed."}
{"trans": "Even the most significant events that span a thousand years, or the most magnificent achievements that stretch for thousands of miles, if they are part of a culture, are often borne by a pair of aged shoulders. Like smugglers or fugitives, they move stealthily, conducting covert investigations in search of a place to entrust their responsibilities. The decision to entrust something is always written in a will; therefore, it is doomed to never be possible to explain the cultural significance of one’s life while still alive."}
{"trans": "There’s no doubt about the outcome: overgrown grass and broken tiles bear the marks of disasters that have occurred throughout the ages. I’m willing to face all of this in a perilous situation without any protective measures, just as I would remove my gloves to touch the scars on an elderly person’s body. Such contact often leads to profound reflection: as the foundation of our existence, Chinese civilization is also riddled with scars—how has it managed to avoid a complete collapse?"}
{"trans": "Is there really anyone who can wrap the meaning that has been created into a birth certificate and give it to you along with the birth certificate itself? The act of being born itself already entails asking the person who is born for meaning. Having to search for or create that meaning is like a publishing contract with the payment for the manuscript already advanced, valid for a lifetime. Of course, you are not the creditor; you are the debtor. It is life that demands meaning from you, so it’s not your place to complain about anyone."}
{"trans": "Those uneven ink stains, those red-lettered headings, those names crossed out, those rows of exclamation marks, those restrained complaints, those repeated alterations—all combine to create a terrifying auditory experience that hits you right in the face. It’s like how a few strands of white hair on a spider’s web in a corner of the room, or a piece of torn cloth among the withered leaves at the top of a tree, can instantly transport us back to an era we dare no longer think about."}
{"trans": "Some fall onto the haircoils of the women picking vegetables, some stick to the black coats of the swallows, and others slide into the small rivers to play in the water. The river, like a thousand wandering musicians playing flutes, accompanies the songs of the children coming home from school. When mischievous children put their books on top of their yellow hats and cross the river with both shoes in hand, could the spore-bearing “babies” perhaps escape from the flutes and bite onto the corners of their clothes, only to eventually return to the soil of their wild fern “mother”?"}
{"trans": "“Soul, return to your old home.” Why didn’t he defend himself when he spoke Minnan dialect and made everyone laugh heartily, or when he spoke Beijing dialect and left them staring at each other in confusion? Here, his Chǔ accent is as profound as the heavens, the earth, and the mountains and rivers; it is as majestic as the gods and spirits. Every word he uttered sounded just like his father reading the “Memorial on Expressing Feelings” – melodious yet filled with sorrow, and each word struck a deep blow to the listener."}
{"trans": "He was too thin; his withered skin couldn’t fill the gaps between his ribs, so his chest resembled a steel bridge spanning over them. His heart beat violently and heavily, like a bleeding sun that burned emptily, emitting flames and the sounds of a cave. Mei Ying had heard Yue Bei’s heartbeat before—it was deep and resonant, and through his well-developed muscles, it sounded like coal buried deep within the earth’s crust, beating steadily and with a strong rhythm."}
{"trans": "From one inn to another, a person who never settles in the mountains or by the waters—what talisman could I pray for? Perhaps it’s youth, but how fleeting it is. I’m like someone who has discovered a treasure; carrying pearls, gold, and silver in a careless net bag, only to realize that the weight lessens as I move on, for youth has already turned to dust. Or perhaps it’s the scriptures and ancient texts, but how can profound knowledge mend the broken mirror in my hands?"}
{"trans": "In the mountain valleys of my hometown, one has to call out from a distance to greet someone. It’s definitely not the soft, gentle “Ah—” used by city dwellers, nor the exaggeratedly surprised “Wa—” common among people from the south. Such sounds travel only a short way before being swallowed by the mountains. Only the deep, resonant, and lingering “Eh Ha—” can soar high like an eagle for a long time. Now, this cry descends from the sky like mist, and an endless sense of nostalgia fills Shen Zhanping’s heart with both warmth and a burning emotion."}
{"trans": "Hurry and escape from the political quagmire that you yourself have not yet come to understand, and pursue the poetic essence that has been lost for so long. To pursue the poetic essence is to pursue the self—the self that was once familiar to the nine provinces, the self that was held tightly by your wife, the self that you thought you had found but instead lost. On this journey of retracing the path, there is the morning glow to accompany you, the rivers to bear witness, the cries of monkeys to encourage you, and the mountains to make way for you. Thus, the ship of life, which has become increasingly heavy, once again turns into a light boat."}
{"trans": "Although airplanes can be likened to Zhuangzi’s carefree journeys or Liezi’s rides on the wind, they are not particularly visually appealing. In contrast, trains offer a different experience: their rhythmic, hypnotic movement, and the ever-changing scenery provide a sense of both being in the mundane world and stepping out of it. When traveling abroad, wherever the tracks extend, I always stand on the platform—a true “long pavilion”—waiting for the majestic train to thunder into the station, ready to take me to distant places."}
{"trans": "In contrast to the prominent and influential, there is the ordinary; in opposition to the officialdom, there are the common people. What offers greater concealment than the dense vegetation and towering trees in the mountains and forests is the everyday life of these commoners, who blend into the fabric of a small town. The concealment in the mountains and forests still retains and embodies a certain sense of prideful solitude, but such prideful concealment is ultimately insincere. In contrast, the concealment in the streets of a small town does not require the deliberate torment or destruction of life; it allows one to live a very comfortable existence, fitting into a quiet and convenient corner, almost allowing one to dissolve completely from the outside in. Therefore, it represents the highest form of concealment. Perhaps calling it merely “concealment” is too narrow-minded. In any case, in my eyes, the scenes of small bridges over flowing waters, homes nestled among the trees, and the thoughts of water shield ferns and perch represent an ecological image of a religious philosophy of life."}
{"trans": "The spring breeze doesn’t recognize me; why does it enter my silk curtains?"}
{"trans": "From then on, I lost all interest in the beautiful nights, letting the bright moon shine as I descended the western tower."}
{"trans": "The candle, with a heart full of emotion, laments the parting; it weeps for others until dawn breaks."}
{"trans": "Chang’e must regret having stolen the elixir of immortality; her heart yearns every night under the azure sea and the green sky."}
{"trans": "Three visits showed great concern for the affairs of the state; two reigns witnessed the loyalty of a devoted minister."}
{"trans": "A tripartite division of power requires clever strategizing; through the ages, it remains but a single feather in the vast sky."}
{"trans": "A tune from the flowers in the back garden, so melancholic and sorrowful that it’s unbearable to listen to."}
{"trans": "In the old days, swallows from the mansions of the royal and noble families would fly into the homes of ordinary people."}
{"trans": "Melancholy without a reason arises when I think of Fan Li; the misty trees stand unevenly to the east of the Five Lakes."}
{"trans": "If the east wind had not favored Zhou Yu, the two Qiao sisters would have been locked away in their bronze sparrow tower for all spring."}
{"trans": "Victory or defeat are matters of war that cannot be anticipated; it is a true man's duty to bear shame and humiliation with courage."}
{"trans": "How can one become the Son of Heaven over the course of four dynasties, when even the Lu family doesn’t have someone like Mo Chou?"}
{"trans": "The tooth-shaped jade token bids farewell to the imperial palace; armored cavalry surrounds the Dragon City."}
{"trans": "Why should the Qiang flute complain about the willows? The spring breeze does not reach the Jade Gate Pass."}
{"trans": "After a hundred battles in the yellow sand, their golden armor is worn out; they will not return until Loulan is conquered."}
{"trans": "The moon shone in the Qin dynasty, the passes stood firm in the Han dynasty; those who embarked on the long march of ten thousand miles have yet to return."}
{"trans": "The soldiers stationed at the border gaze at the distant lands; their longing for home brings many expressions of sorrow to their faces."}
{"trans": "To shoot a man, first shoot his horse; to capture a thief, first capture his leader."}
{"trans": "The vast sea is covered with ice hundreds of feet thick;  \nMournful clouds loom darkly, stretching for thousands of miles."}
{"trans": "The woods are dark, the grass stirs in the wind; the general draws his bow at night."}
{"trans": "The desert sand is like snow; the moon over Yanshan Mountain resembles a hook."}
{"trans": "Weeding under the scorching sun at noon; sweat drips onto the soil beneath the crops."}
{"trans": "A rider in the dust, the queen smiles; no one knows it's lychees that are being brought."}
{"trans": "A horse with a colorful coat, a fur coat worth a thousand gold pieces—call the boy to bring them out and exchange them for fine wine. Let’s drink together and drown our eternal sorrows."}
{"trans": "To cross the Yellow River, the ice blocks the way;\nTo ascend the Taihang Mountains, the snow covers them all."}
{"trans": "When the emperor called for him, he would not board the ship; he claimed to be a immortal in the world of wine."}
{"trans": "Nature has bestowed its divine beauty; yin and yang divide the dawn from the dusk."}
{"trans": "I possess spells of bewilderment, but they cannot be cast; with the crow of a rooster, the world turns white."}
{"trans": "Contemplating the vastness of heaven and earth, I am filled with sorrow and tears roll down my cheeks."}
{"trans": "Boundless fallen leaves rustle down; the endless Yangtze River flows on and on."}
{"trans": "With the spring breeze bringing joy, the horse's hooves speed along; in a single day, one can see all the flowers of Chang'an."}
{"trans": "Zhuangzi dreamed in the morning and was confused by the butterflies; the Emperor of Spring entrusted his feelings to the cuckoo."}
{"trans": "A lone column of smoke rises straight from the desert; the sun sets over the endless river, casting a round glow."}
{"trans": "Sitting alone in the secluded bamboo grove, I play the zither and let out a long, mournful cry."}
{"trans": "The waterfall plunges three thousand feet down; it seems as if the Milky Way has fallen from the ninth heaven."}
{"trans": "The window frames the western mountains covered with snow for a thousand autumns; by the door lie ships from the Eastern Wu, traveling for thousands of miles."}
{"trans": "The chaotic flowers are about to dazzle one’s eyes; only the short grass can conceal the horse’s hooves."}
{"trans": "Four hundred and eighty temples of the Southern Dynasties, how many towers and pavilions stand amidst the mist and rain..."}
{"trans": "During the Qingming Festival, the rain falls incessantly; the pedestrians on the roads seem to have their souls broken."}
{"trans": "I wonder who cut out those delicate leaves so precisely; the spring breeze in February is like a pair of scissors."}
{"trans": "In the human world, the beauty of April fades away; yet in the mountain temples, the peach blossoms begin to bloom in full splendor."}
{"trans": "Even if we are separated by the vast ocean, as long as we have true friends in our hearts, we feel as if we are neighbors."}
{"trans": "If relatives and friends in Luoyang ask about me, my heart is as pure as ice, contained within a jade pot."}
{"trans": "I urge you to drink one more cup of wine; once you pass the Yangguan Pass to the west, there will be no old friends left."}
{"trans": "I entrust my worries to the bright moon, and let it accompany you all the way to the west of Yelang."}
{"trans": "The waters of Taohuatan are a thousand feet deep, yet they cannot compare to the depth of Wang Lun’s affection for me."}
{"trans": "The solitary sail fades into the distance, disappearing into the blue sky; all that remains is the Yangtze River flowing towards the horizon."}
{"trans": "The vast bamboo forest temple, with its distant bell sounds at dusk..."}
{"trans": "As one approaches their hometown, feelings of trepidation grow; they dare not ask the people who have come there."}
{"trans": "Hearing the sound of the willow being broken in this nocturnal piece, who could not be moved with feelings of longing for their hometown?"}
{"trans": "Beacon fires have lasted for three months; a letter from home is worth more than a thousand pieces of gold."}
{"trans": "Who says that the heart of a tiny blade of grass can repay the warmth of the spring sun?"}
{"trans": "The sound of the flute comes from among the reeds as promised, and suddenly a flock of white birds takes flight in panic."}
{"trans": "The pioneer stands at the forefront of the waves, holding a red flag whose colors remain unsoaked."}
{"trans": "Numerous and dense, along roads in all directions: north, south, east, and west."}
{"trans": "Beyond the misty green willows, the morning chill is mild; on the branches of the red apricot trees, the signs of spring are in full bloom."}
